<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adour</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Adour is a river of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, about 300 km long, rising in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> near the Tourmalet pass and flowing through Bigorre, the Landes and Dax to the Atlantic at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayonne">Bayonne</a>. In antiquity its valley was home to Aquitanian peoples such as the Bigerriones and Tarbelli, and its mouth gives Bayonne its port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adour.jpg" alt="Adour" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mheberger · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adour_river_watershed.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
